message: >-
  If you use or discuss this research framework, please cite this repository.
type: software
title: 'Subjective Structural Intelligence (SSI): From Scoring Forests to Perception, Agency, Self-Models, and Worldview Evolution'
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe
  - name: GPT-Obot
    affiliation: OpenAI AI assistant (collaborative contribution)
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sizhet/Subjective-Structural-Intelligence'
url: 'https://github.com/sizhet/Subjective-Structural-Intelligence'
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-19'
abstract: >-
  Subjective Structural Intelligence (SSI) is a proposed research framework
  for studying subject-relative perception, embodied boundaries, historical
  identity, valuation, structural agency, self-referential evaluation, and
  governed worldview evolution. It investigates whose world is modeled,
  whose criteria guide scoring, and whose authority governs choices and
  revisions. SSI distinguishes operational subject models from phenomenal
  consciousness and does not claim empirical validation of consciousness.
keywords:
  - Subjective Structural Intelligence
  - Structural Intelligence
  - Scoring Forest
  - Subject-Relative Valuation
  - Structural Agency
  - Self-Model
  - Metacognition
  - Worldview Evolution
  - AI Governance
  - Historical Identity
